          "testIds": [
            "bank.access.client.ClientSpec.a staff check and a refusal land on bank access-decisions, and a customer seeing their own does not()",
            "bank.access.client.ClientSpec.an owner may, a stranger may not, one acting may only with a grant, and a request asks each question once()",
            "bank.access.client.ClientSpec.every relation the client names is one the model has, so a renamed relation fails the build()",
            "bank.access.client.ClientSpec.with OpenFGA stopped, or slower than the budget, every check is unanswered, which is a 503, and counted()",
            "bank.access.fga.CarriedHeadersTest.every call sends the headers the caller carries, the store's lookup included()",
            "bank.access.sync.LevelFileSpec.DEBUG in the file turns its own lines to DEBUG, and INFO turns them back()",
            "bank.access.sync.LevelFileSpec.a file that is missing, or names no level, changes nothing()",
            "bank.access.sync.LogJsonSpec.a line, its MDC and its exception are one JSON object with the shared fields()",
            "bank.access.sync.SyncSpec.an emptied store, rebuilt from offset zero and Pocket ID, answers every check as it did before()",
            "bank.access.sync.SyncSpec.an opened account's owner sees it, an approved grant lets Bob see it until it expires, and a group is its members()",
            "bank.access.sync.TracedSyncSpec.an account published inside a trace has its owner written to OpenFGA in a span of that trace()",
            "checks.access.adapters.AccessSpec.Access - a session signed out of, or never opened, says nobody",
            "checks.access.adapters.AccessSpec.Access - a sign-in finished in another browser, finished twice, or finished too late is refused",
            "checks.access.adapters.AccessSpec.Access - a sign-in only ever returns to a page of the check",
            "checks.access.adapters.AccessSpec.Access - someone in none of the admins' groups is refused, and given no session",
            "checks.access.adapters.AccessSpec.Access - someone the provider puts in an admins' group signs in, back where they were, and their session says who",
            "checks.access.adapters.OidcProviderSpec.ID tokens - one for another client, for another sign-in, or from another issuer is refused",
            "checks.access.adapters.OidcProviderSpec.ID tokens - one the provider signed for this client, with the sign-in's nonce, names the person and their groups",
            "checks.admin.AdminApiSpec.The admin API - a draft naming a field its record lacks is checked, not stored",
            "checks.admin.AdminApiSpec.The admin API - a rule over movements is dry-run as the evaluator counts, and made live",
            "checks.admin.AdminApiSpec.The admin API - a rule over transfers is drafted, read, tried, dry-run and made live, and then declines the next one",
            "checks.admin.AdminApiSpec.The admin API - nothing is read or written without signing in",
            "checks.app.AppSpec.The app - it is healthy, describes /screen in its OpenAPI document, and measures each screening",
            "checks.app.LogJsonSpec.LogJson - the app's lines, and its libraries', are JSON objects, and an annotation is a field of its own",
            "checks.app.MigrationsSpec.Migrations - migrate applies every context's migrations once, and a second run applies none",
            "checks.app.MigrationsSpec.Migrations - the app refuses to start on a database migrate has not run on, naming what is pending",
            "checks.app.OpenApiSpec.The OpenAPI document - the committed openapi.json is the one the check serves",
            "checks.app.WizardSpec.The wizard - an admin writes a rule of two groups with a negation, reads it, tries it, and makes it live",
            "checks.app.WizardSpec.The wizard - someone the provider puts in none of the admins' groups is refused, and given no session",
            "checks.bankevents.AccountEventsSpec.Account events - a consumer stopped mid-run and started again leaves no event unchecked",
            "checks.bankevents.ApprovalEventsSpec.Approval events - a request rejected, withdrawn, superseded or expired ends without approval",
            "checks.bankevents.ApprovalEventsSpec.Approval events - another kind's events, and the record's own, are not the check's to act on",
            "checks.bankevents.ApprovalEventsSpec.Approval events - approval given, automatically or by people, is a decision for the content it names",
            "checks.bankevents.HandledSpec.Handled - an event published in a trace is handled in a consumer span whose parent is the publish",
            "checks.bankevents.HandledSpec.Handled - an event published in no trace is handled in none",
            "checks.bankevents.MovementsSpec.Movements - a debit's reference is its transfer",
            "checks.bankevents.MovementsSpec.Movements - a record framed as the bank frames it reads back as the movement it was",
            "checks.bankevents.MovementsSpec.Movements - a record not framed is refused, not misread",
            "checks.bankevents.MovementsSpec.Movements - an event of a kind added after this build passes without a word",
            "checks.bankevents.MovementsSpec.Movements - every account event kind becomes the right movement, or none",
            "checks.monitoring.domain.FlagSpec.Flag - protoc's classes read every Flag zio-schema writes, field for field",
            "checks.monitoring.domain.FlagSpec.Flag - the flags' schema breaks nothing published before it",
            "checks.policy.adapters.ApprovingSpec.Asking Approvals - a first version tightens, whatever its reach; a new condition reaching as far reshapes",
            "checks.policy.adapters.ApprovingSpec.Asking Approvals - a refused version is never in force, and the one before it stays",
            "checks.policy.adapters.ApprovingSpec.Asking Approvals - a version made live waits, asked about with what it changes, and is in force only once approval is given",
            "checks.policy.adapters.ApprovingSpec.Asking Approvals - an approval of other content is refused, and one heard twice is answered twice and applied once",
            "checks.policy.adapters.ApprovingSpec.Asking Approvals - switching a low rule off is asked as a switch-off, and a draft is stored without asking",
            "checks.policy.adapters.PostgresVersionsSpec.Postgres versions - a rule over transfers cannot become a rule over movements",
            "checks.policy.adapters.PostgresVersionsSpec.Postgres versions - a version stored by one node is live on another within a second",
            "checks.policy.adapters.PostgresVersionsSpec.Postgres versions - switching a rule off keeps its history",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a draft leaves the live version in force",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a draft naming a field its record lacks is refused with that error",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a draft over the record's own fields is its rule",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a draft reading a text field as a number is refused",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a rule over movements cannot read a proposed transfer's fields",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a rule switched off has no live version, and keeps every version it had",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a rule's latest live version is the one in force",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - a version waiting for approval, or refused it, leaves the version before it in force",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - live rules are in the admin's order",
            "checks.policy.domain.PolicySpec.Policy - the hash of what is asked is Approvals' own: before, after and facts, the facts in key order",
            "checks.policy.domain.RecordsSpec.Records - a rule over a movement can read each of its fields",
            "checks.policy.domain.RecordsSpec.Records - a rule over a proposed transfer can read each of its fields",
            "checks.screening.adapters.ScreeningHttpSpec.POST /screen - a second request for a transfer answers the first decision, though the rules have changed",
            "checks.screening.adapters.ScreeningHttpSpec.POST /screen - a transfer over the bound is declined by the rule, in the bank's words",
            "checks.screening.adapters.ScreeningHttpSpec.POST /screen - an amount that is not a number is refused",
            "checks.screening.adapters.ScreeningHttpSpec.POST /screen - p99 over 10,000 requests is under 20 ms",
            "checks.screening.adapters.TracedSpec.Traced - a request in a trace is answered in a server span whose parent is the caller's",
            "checks.screening.adapters.TracedSpec.Traced - a request with no trace starts one of its own",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - a decline names the rule and version, with verdict's evidence",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - a declining rule declines exactly the transfers its bounds say",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - a preview weighs every live rule, and decides as the check would",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - a rule reads the hour the transfer was requested, in UTC",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - the first rule in the admin's order that holds declines",
            "checks.screening.domain.ScreenSpec.Screen - with no rule live, every transfer is approved"
          ]
        }
